# AI CLI & Memory Folders
# NOTE: NOTHING under .claude/ is ignored any more except throwaway backups. The rule files
# (.claude/rules/*.md, path-scoped), .claude/settings.json (the enforcement hooks) and
# .claude/settings.local.json (permissions) are all deliberately TRACKED. A blanket `.claude/` would
# silently stop new rule files from being committed. `.remember/` and `.superpowers/` are local skill
# scratch (never were tracked) -- fine to ignore (confirmed 2026-07-24).
# settings.local.json was un-ignored 2026-07-28 13:10 EDT (Harkirat's call): it is the last piece of
# the Claude-Code config that was unrecoverable, it holds only permission strings (verified: no
# secrets, and the repo is private), and tracking it means a fresh clone gets the whole working setup.
# Expect churn -- Claude Code rewrites this file whenever a permission is granted.
# ⚠️ Secrets still NEVER go in .claude/ -- `.env` remains the hard invariant (see CLAUDE.md).
# ⚠️ The repo-level entry alone was NOT enough: `~/.config/git/ignore` (the GLOBAL excludes file)
# carries `**/.claude/settings.local.json`, which ignores it in EVERY repo on this machine. Editing
# that global file would silently change behaviour for every other project, so the un-ignore is scoped
# here with an explicit negation — a repo `.gitignore` outranks the global excludes file. Found with
# `git check-ignore -v` 2026-07-28 13:10 EDT, after removing the local pattern left it still ignored.
!.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.bak*
.claude/*.bak
.claude/*.bak-*
.remember/
.superpowers/


